<title>ESTONIA: NORMA GROUP APPROVES BONUS SHARE ISSUE.</title>
<headline>NORMA GROUP APPROVES BONUS SHARE ISSUE.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norma Group shareholders approved its profit distribution and bonus share issue on Friday evening, the company said.</p>
<p>&quot;The shareholders decided to pay dividends of 25 percent of the share par value,&quot; Juri Kao, Norma Group council member, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Norma Group had a net profit of 50 million kroons in 1996 and it will pay 5.5 million kroons for dividends and retain the rest.</p>
<p>The shareholders approved the bonus share issue under which the present share capital of 22.1 million kroons will grow to 110.7 million kroons.</p>
<p>Norma Group shareholders are individuals.</p>
<p>Norma, a diversified industrialist, is traded on the free market of Tallinn Stock Exchange, and is part of Norma Group.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
